        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. For each nonempty oriented regular link diagram K, let w(K) be its determinant writhe and c(K) its number of components, and define D,L,F by the conventions stated for this page. Then D_K(a,z)=-i^{-w(K)}(-1)^{c(K)}L_K(ia,-iz), with i^2=-1. The value assigned to L is independent of reversing the orientation of any whole component. The Dubrovnik value has the stated difference-skein, curl and circle rules; the Kauffman value has the sum-skein, curl and circle rules; and F_K(A,Z)=A^{-w(K)}L_K(A,Z) is unchanged by planar isotopy and every oriented Reidemeister move of types I, II, and III. The claim concerns these finite diagram moves and uses the universal coefficient relations without dividing by a skein variable."
